# Build artifacts. `target/` is never garbage-collected by Cargo, so it is also
# the thing that grows without bound — see docs/researches/18 §3.7.
/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Per-crate and per-tool artifact trees. ⚠️ **Neither of the two paths below is
# written by anything**, and they are kept as a guard rather than described as
# a fact: `cargo-llvm-cov` builds into `target/llvm-cov-target` on its own, and
# `check-coverage.sh` deliberately sets no `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` because doing so
# overrode the one the negative suite's fixtures configure. `mutants.sh` uses
# `target/mutants` and `target/mutants-tmp` — all three already covered by
# `/target/`. The two entries below are siblings of `target/` and so are not;
# they only matter if someone points a tool at the repository root instead.
/target-cov/
/target-mutants/
# cargo-mutants writes its report tree here, and rotates the previous one.
# ⚠️ It contains absolute paths, the hostname and the username — `lock.json`
# carries all three. `M0.17` staged 572 of these files before review caught it.
/mutants.out/
/mutants.out.old/

# Test scratch. Everything lands under target/ so `cargo clean` reclaims it and
# nothing touches the system temp dir, which is a 16 GB tmpfs on WSL2.
# docs/researches/18 §3.7.4.
/target/tmp/

# Per-commit review artifacts, keyed by staged-diff hash. Regenerable by
# re-running the reviewer, and consumed on the machine that made them; the gate
# recomputes the hash rather than trusting the file. docs/researches/21 §5.
#
# ⚠️ **Milestone** review artifacts are not here — they are tracked, in
# `reviews/`. Coverage of a milestone is a durable claim about history that a
# fresh clone and CI have to be able to check, and it is not regenerable
# without an agent re-reading the whole milestone. See the note at the top of
# scripts/check-milestone-review.sh.
/target/review/

# Fuzzing
/fuzz/target/
/fuzz/corpus/
/fuzz/artifacts/

# Editor / OS
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Secrets. Nothing here should ever exist, but a gate that never fires costs
# nothing and the one time it fires it saves a rotation.
*.pem
*.key
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Python bytecode from scripts/lib/, imported by the gates. `M1.32`.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
